# Git commits — human authorship only

When creating commits (only when the user explicitly asks), **never** attribute authorship to AI tools or add co-author trailers.

## Author identity

- Use the repo's existing git config (`user.name`, `user.email`) — **do not** change git config.
- **Never** pass `--author`, `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME`, `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL`, `GIT_COMMITTER_NAME`, or `GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL` to impersonate Cursor, Claude, Composer, Copilot, or similar.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` / `Co-Authored-By:` trailers — **any** co-author (human pair-programmer or AI). This repo uses single-author commits only.

## Commit message & description

- **Never** mention Cursor, Composer, Claude, AI, or "generated by" in the subject, body, or PR description you draft.
- **Never** add `Generated with Claude Code` or Cursor PR/commit footers.
- Write commit messages as the human developer would: what changed and why, in conventional-commit style when the repo uses it.

## Daily batch commits

Use the **`batch-commit`** skill (`.cursor/skills/batch-commit/SKILL.md`):

- **`/batch-commit N`** = **N commits per session**, each **5–10 files** — not N giant commits for the whole tree.
- **Before and after** a batch session, run **`bun run ci:quality`** (same checks as `ci.yml` / `cd-dev.yml` quality) — ESLint errors, type-check, filenames, build.
- Stop after N commits; leave remaining changes uncommitted for the next day.
- Never `git add -A` on a large dirty tree unless the user explicitly asks to commit everything at once.

## Examples

```text
❌ Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
❌ Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
❌ feat: add inbox (via Cursor)
❌ 10 commits × 200 files each (whole refactor in one day)

✅ feat: add guest inbox thread list (4 files)
✅ /batch-commit 10 → 10 small commits today, ~50–100 files total
```

## Repo enforcement

- **`scripts/dev/strip-commit-co-author-trailers.sh`** strips all `Co-authored-by` lines and common AI attribution footers.
- **`.husky/commit-msg`** runs that script before commitlint.
- **`.claude/settings.json`** sets `attribution.commit` / `attribution.pr` to empty strings (Claude Code CLI).
- Skill: **`git-commits`** (`.agent/skills/git-commits/SKILL.md`).

## Cleaning history

If trailers are already on pushed commits, run **`scripts/dev/strip-co-authors-from-history.sh`** (clean tree required), then **`git push --force-with-lease`** only when the user asks to update the remote.
